    "text": "Ic hine generie & his n\u00e6m\u00e6n swilce gewuldrige geond e\u00e6lle weor\u00f0eod\u00e6 & him lifd\u00e6g\u00e6s & l\u00e6nge\nGod is \u00f0et m\u00e6n drihtne & ge\u00e6r\u00e6 \u00e6ndette & neodlice his n\u00e6m\u00e6n \u00e6singe \u00feone he\u00e6hest\u00e6n hele\u00f0\u00e6\nAnd \u00feonne on morgenne megenne sege hu he milde we\u00e6r\u00f0 m\u00e6nn\u00e6 cynne & his so\u00f0e sege ne\u00e6htes.\nWet ic on tin strengum getogen hefde hu ic \u00f0e on s\u00e6lterio sing\u00e6n me\u00e6hte o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00fee mid he\u00e6rp\u00e6n\nHu micle sint \u00feine megenweorc me\u00e6htig drihten werun \u00f0ine ge\u00f0\u00e6nc\u00e6s \u00feearle deope.\nWonhidig wer \u00f0es wiht ne ce\u00e6n ne \u00fe\u00e6s \u00e6ndgyt h\u00e6f\u00e6d \u00e6nig disigr\u00e6.\n\u00deonne for\u00f0 cum\u00e6\u00fe firenfulr\u00e6 \u00f0re\u00e6t he\u00e6p sinningr\u00e6 hige onlic e\u00e6lle \u00f0\u00e6r \u00e6tyw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6 \u00f0e unriht\u00e6s on\n\u00deu on ecnesse \u00e6w\u00e6 drihten he\u00e6hste bist hefonrices we\u00e6rd.\n\u00dei nu \u00f0inre feond f\u00e6cne drihten on eor\u00f0wege e\u00e6lle forweor\u00f0\u00e6\u00f0 & weor\u00f0\u00e6\u00fe towrecene wide e\u00e6lle \u00f0\u00e6\n\u00deonne \u00e6nhorn\u00e6 e\u00e6lr\u00e6 gelic\u00e6st min horn weor\u00f0e\u00f0 \u00e6h\u00e6fen swi\u00f0e & mine yldo beo\u00f0 \u00e6ghwer\n\u00c6nd e\u00e6g\u00e6 \u00f0in eac sceawade hwer fynd mine f\u00e6cne wer\u00e6n & mine wergend wr\u00e6\u00f0e gehirde efne \u00f0in\nSe so\u00f0fest\u00e6 s\u00e6med anlic\u00e6st beorht on bl\u00e6dum blowe\u00f0 sw\u00e6 p\u00e6lm\u00e6 & sw\u00e6 Lib\u00e6nes beorh lide\u00f0 &\nSett\u00e6\u00fe nu georne on godes huse \u00feet ge on his wicum wel geblowen.\nNu gyt sind\u00e6n m\u00e6nige m\u00e6nn\u00e6 swilc\u00e6 \u00f0e him yldo gebidan \u00e6r to genihte & \u00fe\u00e6 mid ge\u00f0ilde \u00feend\u00e6n\nCwed\u00e6n \u00feet were so\u00f0fest silua driht\u00e6n & hine unrihtes \u00e6wiht ne heolde.\nDrihten ricsode wlite he scyrdde scrydde drihten strangnesse & he begirde hine of megene & \u00fe\u00e6\nGe\u00e6ru is \u00f0in setl & \u00f0u ece god er worulde frum\u00e6n wun\u00e6st butan ende.\nHof\u00e6n hior\u00e6 stefne stre\u00e6m\u00e6s driht\u00e6n, hof\u00e6n & hlyns\u00e6d\u00e6n hlud\u00e6n reord\u00e6 fr\u00e6m weterstefnum\nWreclice synd\u00e6n wege\u00e6 g\u00e6ng\u00e6s \u00feonne s\u00e6stre\u00e6m\u00e6s swi\u00f0ust flow\u00e6\u00f0 sw\u00e6 is wundorlic we\u00e6ldend\n\u00dein gewitnes is drihten weorcum gele\u00e6fsum & mid so\u00f0e is swi\u00f0e getrew\u00e6\u00fe.\nHuse \u00feinum h\u00e6lig ged\u00e6fen\u00e6\u00fe drihten usser & d\u00e6g\u00e6s l\u00e6ng\u00e6.\nGod \u00feu eart wrecen\u00e6 god & \u00f0u me\u00e6ht wrec\u00e6n swylce \u00e6na gefreogan \u00e6ghwylcne m\u00e6n.\nAhef \u00f0e on hellen eor\u00f0\u00e6n dem\u00e6 gild oferhidegum sw\u00e6 hi er gr\u00e6m\u00e6 worhton.\nHu l\u00e6nge fyrenwyrht\u00e6n fold\u00e6n we\u00e6lda\u00fe o\u00f0\u00f0e manwyrht\u00e6n mor\u00f0ra gylpa\u00f0.\nHi oftust sprec\u00e6\u00fe unnyt secga\u00f0 & woh meldia\u00f0 wyrce\u00e6\u00fe unriht.\nFolc hi \u00fein drihten f\u00e6cne gehind\u00e6n & yrf\u00e6 \u00f0in e\u00e6ll forcom\u00e6n.\nEall\u00f0eodige men e\u00e6rm\u00e6 widw\u00e6n stiopcild\u00e6 fe\u00e6la stundum acwealdan.\nSegd\u00e6n & cwe\u00f0\u00e6n \u00feet ne ges\u00e6we drihten \u00e6fre dyde sw\u00e6 he wolde ne \u00f0et Iacobes god ongitan cu\u00f0e.\nOnfind\u00e6n \u00f0e\u00f0 & ongeoton \u00fee on folce nu unwiseste e\u00e6lre sindon disige hwethwygu deope \u00feet\nSe \u00f0e erest ealdum earan worhte hu se oferhleo\u00f0ur \u00e6fre wurde & him e\u00e6gana gesih\u00f0 eallum sealde &\nGod e\u00e6lle can guman ge\u00f0ancas eor\u00f0buendr\u00e6 for\u00f0on hi ydle sind.\n\u00de\u00e6t bi\u00f0 e\u00e6dig m\u00e6n \u00f0e \u00f0u hine ece god on \u00feinre so\u00f0re \u00e6 sylfa getihtest & hine \u00feeodscipe \u00feinne\nNefre wi\u00f0drife\u00f0 drihten ure his \u00e6gen folc ne his yrfe \u00f0on ma on ealdre wile hefre forlet\u00e6n.\nHwilc \u00f0onne gena gewerfe\u00fe bi\u00f0 \u00feet he on unriht eft ne oncyrre o\u00f0\u00f0e wilc nime\u00f0 me \u00feet ic man fleo\nHwylc arise\u00f0 mid me \u00feet ic riht fremme & wi\u00f0 awirgdum winne & st\u00e6nde \u00f0e unrihtes e\u00e6lle\nNim\u00f0e me drihten dem\u00e6 usser gefultumed fegere \u00e6t \u00fee\u00e6rfe weninga min saul sohte helle.\nGif ic \u00f0et segde \u00feet min silfes fot ful sarlice asliden were \u00fe\u00e6 me mildheortnes mihtigan drihtnes\n\u00c6fter \u00f0ere m\u00e6nigeo minr\u00e6 sar\u00e6 \u00f0e me \u00e6r \u00e6n ferh\u00f0e feste gestod\u00e6n \u00fe\u00e6 me \u00feine frofre fegere\nNe etfylige\u00f0 \u00fee \u00e6hwer facen ne unriht \u00feu gefestn\u00e6st e\u00e6c facen sares hi so\u00f0feste sniome geheft\u00e6\u00fe &\nFor\u00f0on me is geworden wealdend drihten to fri\u00f0stole fest & gest\u00e6\u00feeled is me fultum his fest on\n\u00deonne him gylde\u00fe god elmihtig ealla \u00fea unriht \u00fee hi gearned\u00e6n & on hiora facne feste todrife\u00f0\nCume\u00f0 nu togedremene uten cweman gode winnum drihten wealdind herigean urum helende hildo\nWutun his ansine arest sece\u00e6n \u00feet we andett\u00e6n ure fyrene & we sealmas him sing\u00e6n mid winne.\nFor\u00f0on is se micla god kining ofer eall manne godu.\nFor\u00f0on ne wi\u00f0drife\u00f0 drihten usser his agen folc \u00e6fre \u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0e\u00e6rfe he \u00fe\u00e6s heahbeorg\u00e6s healde\u00f0 swilce.\nE\u00e6c he se\u00e6s wealde\u00f0 & he sette \u00f0one worhte his folme e\u00e6c fold\u00e6n drige.\nCum\u00e6\u00f0 him fore & cneow bigea\u00f0 on ansine ures drihtnes & him wepan fore \u00f0e us worhte \u00e6r.\nFor\u00f0on he is drihten god dema usser werum we his fele folc & his f\u00e6gere sce\u00e6p \u00fe\u00e6 he on his edisce\nGif ge to dege drihtnes stefne holde gehiran nefre ge heortan ge\u00f0anc deorce forhirdan drihtnes willan.\nSw\u00e6 on grimnesse fyrn ger\u00e6 dydan on \u00f0am wra\u00f0an dege & on westenne \u00feer min \u00f0urh facen federas\nNu ic feowertig folce \u00f0yssum wintra rimes wuned\u00e6 neah aa & simble cwe\u00f0 & e\u00e6c & swa oncneow\nHi weg\u00e6s mine wihte ne oncneowan \u00feet ic er on yrre \u00e6\u00f0e benemde gif hi on mine reste ricene\nSinga\u00f0 nu drihtne sang\u00e6s niowe singe \u00f0eos eor\u00f0e e\u00e6ll eceum drihtne.\nSing\u00e6\u00f0 nu drihtne & his so\u00f0ne n\u00e6m\u00e6n",
